    14	   \[
    15	   \boxed{\sum_{p\in K_f\cup K_g}
    16	   \min\!\left(\left\lfloor\frac{R_p}{\alpha}\right\rfloor,
    17	               \left\lfloor\frac{S_p}{\beta}\right\rfloor\right)^2
    18	   \ge B^2-1.}\tag{PCC}
    19	   \]
    20	
    21	   Here the sum is over the canonical proper and infinitely-near base
    22	   cluster in the minimal simultaneous point resolution of the two
    23	   projective pencils.  PCC immediately gives `td <= alpha*beta`.  Unlike
    24	   KME-2, it is not the desired inequality rewritten: it is a formally
    25	   stronger sufficient lemma, with no converse asserted.
