   208	## 5. Branching semantics — where subcases come from
   209	
   210	Branch points, in decreasing frequency (each pushes a labeled node; the
   211	algorithm explores the whole tree; a leaf = emitted case or contradiction):
   212	
   213	B1 **Root partition of a certified R** (step 3). R has z-degree D/qm slots and
   214	   support st(R)→en(R); enumerate partitions t₁ ≥ t₂ ≥ … of the slot count into
   215	   distinct-root multiplicities; filter by R4 (ϑ must appear), R5 (zero root),
   216	   chain data (the major root's multiplicity is fixed by A_{h+1}: mult/m =
   217	   v_{01}(A−A′)/gap when the edge is "simple", GGV5 §3). — Prop 4.2: partitions
   218	   of 3 = {3},{2,1},{1,1,1}; {1,1,1} killed by R4; {2,1} ⇒ subcase (1);
   219	   {3} ⇒ continue. Prop 4.3 second cut: {8·} one-or-two-factor split:
   220	   {2·4m,1·4m}-shape ⇒ case c) vs single ⇒ case b).
   221	B2 **st-candidates after a full collapse** (step 2 re-run). When a cut removes
   222	   an entire edge, the new predecessor start comes from R3's list. — Prop 4.2:
   223	   st ∈ 3m{(0,0),(3,1)} ⇒ subcases (3) and (2). Prop 4.3 first cut:
   224	   Pred ∈ {(1,−3),(2,−7)}: (2,−7) uncuttable ⇒ case a) terminates; (1,−3) ⇒
   225	   continue into B1.
   226	B3 **Aligned vs non-aligned ends** in R9 — in all §4 instances the aligned
   227	   branch dies, but the design must carry it (it may survive in new families).
   228	
   229	Branches that later converge (4.3's a) and b): different tails, same polygons
   230	after R9 supersedes the tails) are merged by hashing the emitted state —
     1	"""SECTION4-AUTOMATION Phase 2: the GGV22 (arXiv:2204.14178) S4 reduction engine.
     2	
     3	Reproduces the per-family Newton-polygon reductions of GGV22 S4 (Props 4.1-4.4)
     4	from Phase 1 CornerData (lib/families.py) alone, per SECTION4-AUTOMATION.md:
     5	
     6	  R1  edge-power certificates  (GGV1 = arXiv:1401.1784 Cor 7.4 `fracciones de
     7	      F1`, flipped frame; q from the (q_k) chain data, R2)
     8	  R3  PossibleStartingPoints   (GGV22 Algorithm 1, verbatim) + Prop 3.12
     9	      case-(1) single-root shapes + the v=0 origin-ray option
    10	  R4  forced-multiplicity filter (GGV2 = arXiv:1605.09430 Prop 3.12
    11	      `finitas direcciones`, all three cases checked as a consistency filter)
    12	  R5  zero-root exclusion for the cut root (support-level)
    13	  R6  x-degree floor (vdE Prop 10.2.6; pre-Laurent states only)
    14	  R7  PLLC membership (families.get_pllc; used by the (8,32)-style discard)
    15	  R8  divisibility of d (GGV1 Thm 7.6(5)/(8); (8,32)-style discard)
    16	  R9  tail resolution (GGV1 Prop 8.2 `esquina de 83` + GGV22's opposite-vertex
    17	      divisibility filter, aligned-branch recursion with colinearity kills)
    18	  R10 finalization psi_j: x -> x^{-1}, y -> x^j y; bracket -> x^(j-2)
    19	
    20	Conventions: the whole reduction runs in FLIPPED coordinates (phi1: x<->y
    21	applied to the GGV5 start polygon), state polygons are 1/m-units lattice
    22	corner lists, SuppP = m*state, SuppQ = n*state until R9 individuates them.
    23	st/en of a face = its endpoints in CCW hull order (GGV1 Notation 1.2:
    24	(rho,sigma) x (en - st) > 0).
    25	
    26	Branch semantics (design S5): B1 root partitions, B2 st-candidates after a
    27	full collapse, B3 aligned ends in R9.  Leaves are merged by hashing the
    28	emitted (N(P), N(Q), rhs).  Unresolvable structure raises Stuck -> status
    29	'stuck' with the state dumped, never a guess.
    30	"""
    31	import sys, os
    32	from fractions import Fraction
    33	from math import gcd
    34	from collections import namedtuple
    35	
    36	sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(__file__))
    37	from families import (CornerData, get_pllc, corner_data, section4_families,
    38	                      enumerate_cases, chain_path, v11)
    39	
    40	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- exceptions
    41	
    42	class Stuck(Exception):
    43	    "engine cannot certify/resolve; carries a state dump (design S6)"
    44	
    45	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- direction order
    46	# Total CCW order on directions starting at (0,-1):
    47	# (0,-1) < (1,-K)... < (1,-1) < (1,0) < (0,1) < (-1,K)... < (-1,0).
    48	
    49	def _dquad(d):
    50	    r, s = d
    51	    assert (r, s) != (0, 0)
    52	    if r == 0:
    53	        return 0 if s < 0 else 4
    54	    if r > 0:
    55	        return 1 if s < 0 else (2 if s == 0 else 3)
    56	    return 5 if s > 0 else (6 if s == 0 else 7)
    57	
    58	def dir_lt(d1, d2):
    59	    "d1 strictly before d2 in the CCW sweep from (0,-1)"
    60	    q1, q2 = _dquad(d1), _dquad(d2)
    61	    if q1 != q2:
    62	        return q1 < q2
    63	    return d1[0] * d2[1] - d1[1] * d2[0] > 0
    64	
    65	def prim(v):
    66	    "primitive vector along v"
    67	    g = gcd(abs(v[0]), abs(v[1]))
    68	    return (v[0] // g, v[1] // g)
    69	
    70	def outdir(edge_vec):
    71	    "outward normal of a CCW polygon edge (dx,dy): (dy,-dx) primitive"
    72	    return prim((edge_vec[1], -edge_vec[0]))
    73	
    74	def vdir(d, p):
    75	    return d[0] * p[0] + d[1] * p[1]
    76	
    77	def cross(u, v):
    78	    return u[0] * v[1] - u[1] * v[0]
    79	
    80	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hull / faces
    81	
    82	def hull(points):
    83	    "convex hull, CCW corner list starting at the lexicographic minimum"
    84	    pts = sorted(set(points))
    85	    if len(pts) == 1:
    86	        return tuple(pts)
    87	    def half(ps):
