   279	## 6. Normalization transport update and the remaining notation break
   280	
   281	### GGV `(m,n)` now transports to Sigray `(alpha,beta)` for the selected pair
   282	
   283	The scan reads `(al,be)` from the Sigray entry generator and stores them in
   284	fields called `m,n` (`cases/tdbound_scan.py:55-66`).  The older promoted
   285	reduction correctly recorded that no dictionary had then been proved
   286	(`REDUCTION.md:315-336`, `:813-824`).  During this review, `TRANSPORT.md` was
   287	added with a stronger pre-Laurent theorem.  Its argument is:
   288	
   289	1. a coordinate polynomial cannot have weighted initial form divisible by
   290	   the coprime cusp binomial `d^r U^s-c^s V^r` (Theorem 1.1, via the
   291	   Hamiltonian locally nilpotent derivation);
   292	2. therefore no target coordinate can cancel the common cusp peak of the two
   293	   rectangular components, giving an exact target-degree formula and
   294	   orbitwise lexicographic minimality (Theorem 2.1); and
   295	3. determinant-one target sorting and the source rotation `(x,y)->(y,-x)`
   296	   carry the genuine selected GGV pair to a Sigray-normalized representative
   297	   of type
   298	
   299	   ```text
   300	   (alpha,beta)=(min(m,n),max(m,n)),
   301	   ```
   302	
   303	   with the same `td` and an exactly recoverable pre-Laurent GGV ledger
   304	   (Theorem 3.1 and Section 4).
   305	
   306	I independently checked the algebraic steps above and ran
   307	`python3 cases/transport_check.py`; its actual `(8,28)` GGV fixture transports
   308	from degree pair `(108,72)` to Sigray degree pair `(72,108)` and type `(2,3)`.
   309	This removes the blanket claim that the numerical types are unrelated for the
   310	selected polynomial counterexample.
   311	
   312	It does **not** give GGV provenance to the 23 rows in this review.  The
   313	transport checker has one actual GGV fixture; residue-A and td-7 are explicitly
   314	independent Sigray frame-schema controls, not transports of that fixture.  No
   315	off-axis entry is matched to a GGV admissible chain, and polynomial
   316	realizability remains untracked.  `TRANSPORT.md` also disclaims a
   317	corner-to-tree functor.  The right conclusion is therefore:
   318	
   319	- for a genuine selected GGV counterexample, the proposed law (i) and its
   320	  Sigray version use the same sorted numerical type;
   321	- the 23-row scan remains evidence only about abstract Sigray entry data, not
   322	  23 realized or GGV-certified configurations; and
   323	- the advertised finite-ladder payoff still fails: the GGV enumeration is
