   343	#### Proof
   344	
   345	The target map \(C\) is either the identity or the determinant-one rotation
   346	\((U,V)\mapsto(V,-U)\); it sorts the two multipliers without changing the
   347	normalized base polygon.  Theorem 2.1 proves almost-normalized minimality.
   348	The source map \(R(x,y)=(y,-x)\) also has determinant one and preserves total
   349	degrees, so the rotated representative remains almost normalized and keeps
