   363	## 4. Exact transport of the GGV ledger
   364	
   365	Let \(R^*H=H(y,-x)\), and write
   366	
   367	\[
   368	 T(i,j)=(j,i),\qquad T(\rho,\sigma)=(\sigma,\rho).
   369	\tag{4.1}
   370	\]
   371	
   372	For every polynomial \(H\), every direction \(w=(\rho,\sigma)\), and every
   373	edge with the usual GGV endpoint convention,
   374	
   375	\[
   376	\begin{aligned}
   377	 \operatorname{Supp}(R^*H)&=T\operatorname{Supp}(H),\\
   378	 N(R^*H)&=T N(H),\\
   379	 v_{Tw}(R^*H)&=v_w(H),\\
   380	 \ell_{Tw}(R^*H)&=R^*\ell_w(H),\\
   381	 \operatorname{st}_{Tw}(R^*H)&=T\operatorname{en}_w(H),\\
   382	 \operatorname{en}_{Tw}(R^*H)&=T\operatorname{st}_w(H).
   383	\end{aligned}
   384	\tag{4.2}
   385	\]
   386	
   387	The first four identities follow term by term from
   388	
   389	\[
   390	 x^iy^j\longmapsto(-1)^j x^jy^i,qquad
   391	 (\sigma,\rho)\mathbin\cdot(j,i)=(\rho,\sigma)\mathbin\cdot(i,j).
   392	\]
   393	
   394	The last two reflect the fact that \(T\) reverses orientation on the exponent
   395	lattice.  They can also be checked from GGV's defining inequality
   396	\(w\times(\operatorname{en}-\operatorname{st})>0\).
   397	
   398	In the native repo convention an oriented edge stores
   399	\((A_h,A'_h)=(\operatorname{en}_w,\operatorname{st}_w)\).  There are two
   400	closely related tuples after transport, and they must not be conflated.  The
   401	**label-preserving rational ledger** is the involution
   402	
   403	\[
   404	 (A_h,A'_h;(\rho_h,\sigma_h))
   405	 \longmapsto
   406	 (TA_h,TA'_h;(\sigma_h,\rho_h)).
   407	\tag{4.3}
   408	\]
   409	
   410	The **orientation-preserving endpoint tuple** of the transported leading
   411	face is instead
   412	
   413	\[
   414	 (\operatorname{en}_w,\operatorname{st}_w;w)
   415	 \longmapsto
   416	 (T\operatorname{st}_w,T\operatorname{en}_w;Tw)
   417	 =(TA'_h,TA_h;Tw).
   418	\tag{4.4}
   419	\]
   420	
   421	Thus (4.3) retains the campaign names while (4.4) retains the GGV
   422	`en`/`st` orientation.  In particular, if
   423	\(w\mathbin\times(A_h-A'_h)>0\), then
   424	\((Tw)\mathbin\times(TA'_h-TA_h)>0\), whereas the pointwise ordered pair in
   425	(4.3) has the opposite cross-product sign.
   426	
   427	The GGV5 certificate fraction is unchanged:
   428	
   429	\[
   430	 \frac{\rho_h+\sigma_h}{v_{\rho_h,\sigma_h}(A_h)}
   431	 =
   432	 \frac{\sigma_h+\rho_h}{v_{\sigma_h,\rho_h}(TA_h)}.
   433	\tag{4.5}
   434	\]
   435	
   436	Accordingly its reduced \((p_h,q_h)\) tag is unchanged.  Target rotation
   437	\(C\) only swaps component labels and scalar signs; the normalized base
   438	corners are unchanged because the two component corners are \(mA_h,nA_h\).
   439	Equations (4.1)–(4.5), together with the component label bit, are an explicit
   440	inverse pair of maps.  No native GGV datum is discarded.
   441	
   442	There are two necessary type cautions.
   443	
   444	- Transposition reverses cyclic direction order and swaps `st`/`en`.  A
   445	  direction-ordered display must therefore be reindexed.
   446	- A GGV Laurent corner \((a/l,b)\) may transpose to \((b,a/l)\), which is
   447	  not represented by the repo's x-fraction-only `Corner(a,l,b)` class.  The
   448	  Sigray-side object is a rational valuation ledger, not a claim that all
   449	  fourteen GGV5 admissibility clauses have been re-certified in their native
   450	  chart.  Applying \(T^{-1}\) recovers the certified GGV chain exactly.
   451	
   452	The Sigray representative is formed at the polynomial starting pair, before
   453	**any** GGV5/GGV22 Laurent operation.  Later rational chain corners are
   454	transported only as stored, exactly recoverable ledger metadata.  In
   455	particular, the final maps involving \(x\mapsto x^{-1}\) are not polynomial
   456	source automorphisms and the Proposition 4.3 endpoints have bracket \(x^2\),
   457	not a nonzero constant.  Those reduced strip polygons are not Sigray inputs.
   458	
   459	Finally, (4.2) is not a corner-to-tree functor.  It allows the original GGV
   460	ledger to coexist losslessly with the Eggers–Wall data attached to the
   461	explicit Sigray representative.  It does not say that corner data alone
   462	determine pole status, fiber tags, residual \(g\)-cancellations, or Sigray's
   463	decorations.
