   320	## 4. The window ideal as an ascending chain in the CORE2 ring
   321	
   322	**Gap:** the D25/D27/D-∞ iteration has no theorem. D21 is 13-dimensional
   323	and nonempty mod \(p\); samples die at D23; the pre-registered move is
   324	to emit D25 if D23 is nonempty. That is a grind unless the inverse
   325	system stabilizes.  
   326	**Side:** proof. This is the Noetherianity / saturation argument the
   327	ladder is missing.
   328	
   329	### Five-line pitch
   330	
   331	1. Let \(A\) be the CORE2 coordinate ring after saturating by the pole
   332	   scales: the 27-variable unsplit ring (or the 22-variable fiber ring)
   333	   localized at \(W_1W_2\), i.e. the chart the D21 locus actually lives
   334	   on. This is a finitely generated \(k\)-algebra, hence Noetherian.
   335	2. For each even depth \(D\ge 21\), let \(V_D\) be the window at that
   336	   depth and let
   337	   \(J_D=\ker\bigl(A\to k[V_D]\bigr)\)
   338	   be the elimination ideal of the new tails onto \(A\). Then
   339	   \(J_{21}\subseteq J_{23}\subseteq J_{25}\subseteq\cdots\)
   340	   is an ascending chain in \(A\), and stabilizes at some \(J_{D_*}\).
   341	3. The last twenty-four hours already say the chain *moves* at the
   342	   first step: 0/12 D21 points lie in \(V_{23}\), so those points are
   343	   in \(V(J_{21})\) and not in \(V(J_{23})\), on one prime, as a
   344	   sampling statement. The theorem is that the chain cannot move
   345	   forever.
   346	4. If the deeper tails are integral over \(A\) after saturation (the
   347	   Row_22 block is polynomial in the deep tails, quadratic in highs,
   348	   coefficients in \(A\)), the maps \(V_{D+2}\to V_D\) are finite and
   349	   \(V_\infty=\emptyset\) if and only if some \(V_D=\emptyset\). That
   350	   is the missing implication from “samples die” to “the germ dies.”
   351	5. One Groebner run in a *fixed* ring then replaces the infinite
   352	   ladder: compute \(J_{D_*}\) by eliminating the D23 (then D25, if
   353	   needed) extra tails onto CORE2. If \(J_{D_*}=(1)\), residue-A is
   354	   empty at the window tier as a variety statement, not a sample.
   355	
   356	### Nearest neighbor, and why this is not it
   357	
   358	Mittag-Leffler in `xmodel/sol-avenues2.md` is adjoint compatibility of
   359	the Keller primitive as a meromorphic one-form; it is not an inverse
   360	system of window ideals. Fitting kernels and Hermite–Padé are already
   361	closed or on the board as *row* instruments; they do not name a chain
   362	in a fixed ring. `xmodel/sol-instrument3.md` §4 treats D23/D25 as a
   363	bounded shape census and explicitly warns that “more equations, same
   364	variables” was false on the first reactivation. This idea agrees with
   365	that warning: the new tails are new variables, which is why one must
   366	*eliminate them back* onto \(A\) rather than grind a larger core.
   367	Algkill (`xmodel/sol-algkill.md`) says every D23 *prefix* extends to a
   368	polynomial in the support rectangle; that is about separate
   369	algebraization, not about the ascending chain of joint images.
   370	
   371	### First concrete test
   372	
   373	The D23-core is already on disk:
   374	`cases/directionb_core23_p{105337,105673,200257}.ms`
   375	(38 CORE2 rows + 22 pivots + 10 Row_22 + rad/sat).
   376	
   377	1. Identify the 10 deep-tail variables of Row_22 (levels 49/54).
   378	   Eliminate them, and only them, from the D23-core ideal onto the
   379	   CORE2 variable set. Saturate by \(W_1W_2\) (the `uW` rows already
   380	   make this the chart). Do this at p105337 first; the other two
   381	   primes are the robustness check.
   382	2. Three exact outcomes, all informative:
   383	   - \(J_{23}=(1)\): the D21 image is empty at D23 as a variety. This
   384	     upgrades 0/12 samples to a window-tier kill and is the end of
   385	     the residue-A screening argument (then char-0 of the small
   386	     core).
   387	   - \(J_{23}=(0)\): D23 does not cut the CORE2 base; the sample
   388	     deaths are fiberwise. Then this ambient is the wrong Noetherian
   389	     ring (see kill). Record that, do not pretend the chain moved.
   390	   - \(J_{23}\) proper nonzero: the chain has moved. Compute
   391	     dimension of \(V(J_{23})\) against the known 13. If the cut is
   392	     supported only on the eight near-42 `tg*` frees and leaves the
   393	     five-variable dead-stretch/merge block free, the 13-fold is
   394	     mixed (gauge plus genuine) and the next ambient is the merge
   395	     block's invariant ring.
   396	3. Independent check, no new emission: replay the 12 dead sample
   397	   points against \(J_{23}\). They must lie on \(V(J_{23})\) if
   398	   \(J_{23}\ne(1)\), and must fail to lie on \(V_{21}\) only through
