   405	   the hybrid 87-variable core.
   406	
   407	### Kill criterion
   408	
   409	Kill *this ambient* if \(J_D=(0)\) in \(A\) for every even \(D\) while
   410	random D21 points keep dying at \(D+2\). The conditions then live in
   411	the fibers, not in the CORE2 base. Repair once: enlarge \(A\) by a
   412	finite set of fiber moduli (the 10 deep tails' elementary symmetric
   413	functions, or the invariant ring of the merge block). Kill the
   414	*strategy* if no finite-type ambient works — i.e. if each depth
   415	introduces algebraically independent new tails over every finitely
   416	generated subring of the inverse limit. Algkill's separate-extension
   417	result is then in tension with that conclusion and should be re-read
   418	before declaring the inverse system non-Noetherian. A stabilization
   419	that leaves a positive-dimensional \(V(J_{D_*})\) is not a kill: it
   420	is the actual germ locus, and the ladder has become a theorem about
   421	that scheme.
