   424	
   425	## 5. Greenberg function: a finite depth decides the formal germ
   426	
   427	**Gap:** the same D-∞ hole, at the level of jet schemes rather than
   428	CORE2 coordinates.  
   429	**Side:** proof. This is why a \(D_*\) exists even if idea 4 picked
   430	the wrong chart.
   431	
   432	### Five-line pitch
   433	
   434	1. Residue-A has a finite coefficient rectangle
   435	   \((\deg_x,\deg_y)=(42,126)\) and \((63,189)\). The space of such
   436	   pairs is an affine space \(X\) of finite type. The window \(V_D\)
   437	   is a locally closed subset of a jet scheme of \(X\) (B-frozen,
   438	   no-log, \(W\ne 0\) are algebraic conditions of bounded degree).
   439	2. Greenberg's theorem: for a scheme of finite type over a field,
   440	   there is a function \(\gamma\) such that a jet of order \(n\)
   441	   lifts to a formal (equivalently, by Artin, algebraic) point if and
   442	   only if it lifts to order \(\gamma(n)\). The images
   443	   \(\pi_{m}(V_\infty)\subseteq V_m\) stabilize in the constructible
   444	   topology.
   445	3. Therefore there exists a finite \(D_*\) such that
   446	   \(V_{D_*}=\emptyset\) if and only if \(V_\infty=\emptyset\). The
   447	   depth grind is a computation of \(\gamma\), not an open-ended
   448	   search.
   449	4. The last day already computes the first Greenberg number from
   450	   below: \(\operatorname{im}(V_{23}\to V_{21})\ne V_{21}\) on a
   451	   13-dimensional nonempty base (samples; idea 4 upgrades this to a
   452	   variety statement if \(J_{23}\ne(0)\)). The next number is
   453	   whether \(\operatorname{im}(V_{25}\to V_{21})\) equals
   454	   \(\operatorname{im}(V_{23}\to V_{21})\).
   455	5. Algkill is supporting evidence, not a rival: every *separate* D23
   456	   prefix algebraizes in the rectangle, which is exactly the
   457	   statement that \(X\) is the right finite-type ambient. Joint
   458	   compatibility is the jet-scheme image, which is what Greenberg
   459	   controls.
   460	
   461	### Nearest neighbor, and why this is not it
   462	
   463	Not Mittag-Leffler of the primitive. Not Artin approximation used as a
   464	slogan to “algebraize a D21 point” (the campaign already knows a D21
