   163	polynomials” do not count, because they need not come from one pair.
   164	
   165	**Kill criterion.** Kill the proposed sufficient record if two coherent pairs
   166	on the same fixed fiber have identical enriched \(P/Q\) cut records but
   167	different labelled \(T_a\) images. Also kill it if factor-expanding every
   168	certified GGV chain still misses an infinity branch needed by \(T_a\). Landing
   169	outside the pole subtree is not a failure; it is a correct output whose
   170	finite-\(Q\) status must be retained.
   171	
   172	**Novelty guard.** The dictionary itself is classical. The proposed new object
   173	is its certified application to a coherent paired GGV cut forest with a fiber
   174	tag and a fail-closed pole filter. It claims no Sigray label that the retained
   175	residual data do not determine.
   176	
   177	---
   178	
   179	## 4. Primitive monodromy as a \(td\) bound: blocks or \(A_d/S_d\)
   180	
   181	### Five-line pitch
   182	
   183	1. Choose a counterexample of minimal topological degree \(d\); over the complement of its nonproperness curve it gives a connected finite étale cover with transitive monodromy \(G\le S_d\).
   184	2. Translate a full boundary/book record into inertia permutations and seek a degree-dependent bound \(s(D)\) on their supports and cycle lengths, with \(D=\max(\deg f,\deg g)\).
   185	3. Primitive-group minimal-degree/Jordan theory should then force, above an explicit \(B(D)\), either a nontrivial block system or the exceptional alternatives \(A_d,S_d\).
   186	4. A block system gives an intermediate field; prove that its normalization has an \(\mathbb A^2\) open model and that the induced lower-degree map is again polynomial, Keller, and nonproper.
   187	5. Use discriminant parity to distinguish \(A_d\) from \(S_d\), then exclude the surviving case by an independent boundary/canonical-class constraint, yielding \(td(F)=d\le B(D)\).
   188	
   189	**Why now.** Bézout already gives the uninteresting
   190	\(td\le\deg f\deg g\); the audit needs a bound sharp enough to make a
   191	degree/type theorem and the sheet ladder cooperate. The fat record contains
   192	the local inertia candidates that were previously used only for a fixed
   193	\(S_6\) passport test. Minimal-\(td\) selection makes imprimitivity potentially
   194	fatal, while quantitative primitive-group theory offers a route from bounded
   195	boundary support to a numerical \(B(D)\). There are two explicit new seams,
   196	neither to be hidden: an inertia-support theorem from the geometry, and the
   197	descent of an abstract block quotient back to a polynomial Keller map.
   198	Even success gives a bound in terms of \(D\), not an absolute truncation:
   199	an independent upper bound on \(D\) is still required, and GGV22 supplies a
   200	lower-bound dichotomy rather than that missing upper bound.
   201	
   202	**First concrete test.** Convert every filed survivor through \(td=14\) into
   203	its allowed inertia partitions and enumerate transitive realizations with
   204	passport SAT plus Schreier--Sims. The 169 residue-A passports already known to
   205	admit full \(S_6\) are mandatory negative controls: the test must report
   206	“primitive, no descent,” not invent a block. Then run scalable repeated-\(b\)
   207	and repeated-\(M\) packet families through \(d\le60\), recording minimal
   208	permutation support, forced blocks, and \(A_d/S_d\) survivors as functions of
   209	\(d,D\). On the first forced-block hit, construct the intermediate fixed field
   210	and audit normality, class group, canonical divisor, and polynomiality before
   211	claiming a lower-degree Keller map.
   212	
   213	**Kill criterion.** An infinite scalable family of geometrically admissible
   214	primitive \(A_d\) or \(S_d\) passports with the same proposed degree-controlled
   215	inertia data kills the group-theoretic bound unless the exceptional case is
   216	independently excluded. Even a universally forced block does not prove descent:
   217	one exact example where the intermediate normalization has no
   218	\(\mathbb A^2\) model, or the induced map is not polynomial Keller, kills the
   219	minimality bridge as stated.
   220	
   221	**Novelty guard.** `GROK-MONODROMY.md` asks whether fixed residue-A branch
   222	cycles exist and finds full \(S_6\). This asks an all-\(d\) primitive-group
   223	question, followed by a geometric intermediate-field descent theorem. It is
   224	also deliberately different from the same-day cross-model
   225	Bézout/mixed-volume proposal.
   226	
