   229	## 5. Contextual live-kernel quotient: death before distinction
   230	
   231	### Five-line pitch
   232	
   233	1. Encode simultaneous neutral histories as tuples/shuffles of data words: finite event tags plus their unbounded integer registers, not as words over a falsely finite alphabet.
   234	2. Fix the non-neutral remainder \(C\) and a declared closed symbolic domain for divisibility, cap, coefficient-ideal, and existential-completion predicates; let \(L_C\) be the live encoded histories.
   235	3. Compute symbolic backward preimages of TERM, H8, E5F, tower, merge, and coefficient consumers inside that domain.
   236	4. Quotient two histories only when they have the same full feasible-continuation set, including parameter valuations and provenance before existential projection: a context-indexed residual equivalence for \(L_C\).
   237	5. Finite contextual index would quotient the neutral-history sector only; NF-P cylinders, retained NF-M ideals, and other arithmetic `OPEN`s remain explicit in Rank 2's book.
   238	
   239	**Why now.** The NF-Z counterexamples show that equality of endpoint/product
   240	data does not imply equality of all futures. They do *not* show that a fixed
   241	remaining context can distinguish infinitely many histories before killing
   242	them. The audited td-11 pure-neutral entry contexts supply a planted positive
   243	example: arbitrarily deep co-scaled \(5^k\) tuples die at the same earlier
   244	\(X\), so their later arithmetic is observationally irrelevant there. This
   245	says nothing about the refile, beyond-core, NF-P, or NF-M regions, and symbolic
   246	backward preimages are an algorithmic theorem to prove, not a free consequence
   247	of fixing \(C\).
   248	
   249	**First concrete test.** Build exact backward residuals for the td-11 A/B/C
   250	pure-neutral contexts and derive a single absorbing
   251	`DEAD-before-deep-zone` residual for all \(k\) directly from the existing DIE
   252	horn theorem; direct tuples through depth eight are regression only. As a
   253	mandatory negative control, use a synthetic context that explicitly reads
   254	CE3's flipped first-cap boolean; the quotient must split that pair. Then try
   255	the td-13 2b context, where live intruders should prevent premature collapse.
   256	
   257	**Kill criterion.** An explicit infinite fooling set of pairwise distinguishable
   258	*live* encoded records in one fixed filed context kills finite contextual
   259	index. Failure to close backward preimages in the declared symbolic domain
   260	kills the proposed algorithm even without such a set. Rank 2's exact recursive
   260	kills the proposed algorithm even without such a set. Rank 2's exact recursive
   261	landing book survives either failure.
   262	
   263	**Novelty guard.** NF-D and the td-11 DIE horn already exploit death before
   264	deep history. The new claim is a context-indexed residual construction for
   265	multi-branch data words. It is not `sol-accel2`'s hereditary forbidden-minor
   266	contraction or NF-Z endpoint compression, and its equivalence is intentionally
   267	allowed to change with the consumer context.
   268	
   269	---
   270	
   271	## 6. First-disagreement rigidity for simultaneous neutral words
   272	
   273	### Five-line pitch
   274	
   275	1. Define the exact interleaved consumer ledger for two co-scaled neutral words, including an explicit end-of-word symbol, and first prove that either one-word restriction recovers the Z2 death law.
   276	2. Within one run, consecutive factors \(u,v\) give \(k'=uvP_0/\gcd(uv-1,P_0)\ge uv\ge4\); no cross-branch use is allowed before the interleaving lemma.
   277	3. At the first unequal prefix, add a divisibility edge only when a named competing vertex and exact tower/cap law require that denominator to divide its still-live exponent.
   278	4. On a sector with a proved finite starting cap/divisor set, show that every live mismatch either dies immediately or strictly decreases a registered well-founded divisor state.
   279	5. This bounds only the relative-mismatch skeleton; a synchronized common tail remains an exact symbolic cylinder in Rank 2 and need not have bounded depth.
   280	
   281	**Why now.** CE1--CE3 identify the precise defect in commutative/product-only
   282	normal forms: introducing the same primes in a different order flips later
   283	caps. A genuine multi-branch configuration may be more rigid than an isolated
   284	word because *both* sides must stay alive through those cap changes. The td-11
   285	coupling audit suggests cap shrinkage across its audited branches, but the Z2
   286	formula is presently a one-run statement and general off-axis caps can be
   287	unbounded. The proposal therefore starts with the missing interleaving lemma
   288	and is sector-relative until a finite initial divisor set is proved.
   289	
   290	**First concrete test.** Enumerate all legal pairs of neutral words of depth at
   291	most six in the td-11 and td-13 co-scaling windows, grouped by equal final
   292	\(P/\mu\). Construct the exact cross-cap dependency graph and test whether
   293	each pair that is jointly live by the *raw consumer equations* is equivalent under a fully specified
   294	prefix-divisibility/register relation; no adjacent grouping is declared
   295	harmless in advance. Include all CE1--CE3 anagram pairs as mandatory probes and
   296	record the exact consumer law and first irreversible divisor drop rather than
   297	only a final verdict.
   298	
   299	**Kill criterion.** One exact jointly live mismatch in the registered finite-cap
   300	sector with no decrease in the stated well-founded measure kills the lemma as
   301	stated. An infinite family with unbounded mismatch skeletons kills the broader
   302	avenue even after finite repairs.
   303	
   304	**Novelty guard.** NF-Z† already poses the cross-branch problem, and a prior
   305	idea contracts an already common neutral string. The new content is only the
   306	proposed first-mismatch monovariant plus the interleaved-law bridge; the ordered
   307	fat history is retained until both are proved.
   308	
   309	---
   310	
   311	## 7. Codifferent trace moments on the 126 residue-A conjugates
   312	
   313	### Five-line pitch
   314	
   315	1. Put \(K=\mathbb C(a)(x)\), \(A=K[y]/(f-a)\), \(n=\deg_y(f-a)=126\) in the residue-A orientation, and use the finite-algebra trace rather than choosing a completion branch.
   316	2. The derivation along \(f=a\), \(\delta=\partial_x-(f_x/f_y)\partial_y\), satisfies \(\delta(g)=-1/f_y\) when \(f_xg_y-f_yg_x=1\).
   317	3. Lagrange interpolation gives \(\operatorname{Tr}(h/f_y)=[y^{n-1}](h\bmod(f-a))/a_n(x)\), where \(a_n\) is the \(y\)-leading coefficient.
   318	4. Hence \(\partial_x\operatorname{Tr}(g^r)=-(r/a_n)[y^{n-1}](g^{r-1}\bmod(f-a))\), and in particular \(\partial_x\operatorname{Tr}(g)=0\).
   319	5. These trace/norm recurrences mix all \(f\)-conjugates using the joint coefficients of \(g\), and may expose constraints invisible to separate Hermite--Padé algebraization and Row-24 symbol rank.
   320	
   321	**Why now.** The algebraicity kill failed because every D23 prefix can be
   322	completed *separately*; the trace identity instead consumes the joint Keller
   323	derivation before eliminating the 126 conjugates. It is valid for a finite
   324	separable algebra, so neither irreducibility nor a guessed global branch is a
   325	hidden hypothesis. For
   326	\(Q(Z)=\operatorname{Norm}_{A/K}(Z-g)\), the same calculation gives
   327	differential recurrences for the coefficients of \(Q\) via Newton identities.
   328	This is an elimination instrument, not a claim that a new equation independent
   329	of \(J=1\) has appeared.
   330	
   331	**First concrete test.** Work first at \(a=0\), with \(K_0=\mathbb C(x)\).
   332	Compute the identities by polynomial remainder in \(K_0[y]/(f)\): reconstruct
   333	the joint polynomial \(g\) from its 189-root orbit product and known
   334	\(y\)-leading coefficient, then evaluate \(g(x,y_i)^r\) on the 126
   335	registered roots \(f(x,y_i)=0\), for \(r=1,\ldots,6\), through the D23-known
   336	order. The 189 roots of \(g=0\) are *not* the trace conjugates. Before promising
   337	D23 visibility, audit whether each remainder depends on unpinned B/x or later
   338	tails; a generic \(a\) requires an \(a\)-adic/Hensel deformation of the
   339	\(f-a\) roots. Compare any visible row with the earlier-row ideal at two primes,
   340	then pull it back from the compressed chart and verify it in the original
   341	saturated ring. The exact control \(f=x+y^{126},g=y\) passes;
   342	\(g=y+\epsilon x\) is a non-Keller fail control.
   343	
   344	**Kill criterion.** Kill this as a D23 endgame if every coefficient whose
   345	dependency audit closes at D23 is already a same-depth Jacobian/no-log syzygy
   346	and the first non-syzygetic moment necessarily uses unpinned post-D23 tails.
   347	It may still compress PILOT12, but it is then not an independent obstruction.
   348	
   349	**Novelty guard.** The orbit code uses Newton power sums internally, and the
   350	prior global avenue used Mittag--Leffler pairings on one primitive. Neither
   351	forms the finite-algebra traces of powers of \(g\) nor applies the exact
   352	Lagrange/codifferent identity above.
   353	
   354	---
   355	
   356	## 8. A symbolic \(C_6\) selector recurrence and prolongation test
   357	
   358	### Five-line pitch
   359	
   360	1. Derive the first-occurrence Jacobian operator directly from the orbit-product selector formula with symbolic level \(k=6j+r\), separately for \(r=0,2,4\).
   361	2. Obtain exact character-split matrices \(A_r(j)\) and source terms \(b_r(j)\), including no-log exceptions, instead of interpolating a recurrence from the observed row counts.
   362	3. On each constant-rank chart, compute the full symbol cokernel/Spencer obstruction with preregistered degree and denominator bounds for rational-in-\(j\) identities.
   363	4. A nonzero reduced source defect is a finite compatibility row; vanishing plus unit pivots proves only chartwise prolongability through the regime covered, with determinant-zero strata kept separately.
   364	5. Because the pure-\(y\) regime ends at Row 41, any post-42 claim requires a new symbolic operator containing both x- and y-side variables; otherwise the theorem stops at Row 40.
   365	
   366	**Why now.** `sol-algkill.md` correctly closes the naive claim “Row 24 is a
   367	resonance,” but the proved \(C_6\) support congruence says nothing by itself
   368	about constant symbol dimension or recurrence. The exact selector/product
   369	formula is the only honest place from which a level law could come. This is a
   370	symbolic theorem-discovery pass that uses the Rows 26--40 job now in flight as
   371	regression data; it is not an independent solver lane, the D21 Fitting
   372	compression, or another PILOT12 ordering.
   373	
   374	**First concrete test.** Derive \(A_r(j),b_r(j)\) symbolically for each residue
   375	class and only then regress against
   376	\((24,30,36)\), \((26,32,38)\), and \((28,34,40)\) on every
   377	sign/pole-scale fiber. Row 30 is an explicit exception test because the no-log
   378	pins remove its \(\eta^{29}\) character and that character returns at Row 36.
   379	Reduce the exact Spencer/source defects against the original earlier-row ideal,
   380	cover all selected pivot and rank-drop charts, and make no post-42 extrapolation
   381	until a combined x+y selector formula is derived. A planted triangular family
   382	and a one-row perturbation are controls.
   383	
   384	**Kill criterion.** Kill the recurrence avenue if the selector formula does
   385	not yield bounded-degree rational \(A_r(j),b_r(j)\), if any exact regression row
   386	fails, or if nonlinear source syzygies escape the computed Spencer cokernel.
   387	A chartwise involutive symbol closes only that finite/prescribed regime; it
   388	does not decide post-42 rows or prove that residue-A exists.
   389	
   390	**Novelty guard.** Fitting compression eliminates one finite D21 window, and
   391	the active job generates individual higher rows. This asks for a
   392	selector-derived parameterized symbol and its chartwise Spencer obstruction.
   393	It neither revives the false Row-24 resonance nor presents finite row generation
   394	as an all-orders theorem.
   395	
   396	---
   397	
   398	## Recommended order of attack
   399	
   400	1. Try to break the coordinate-cusp lemma computationally before investing in
   401	   its proof. If it survives, prove it from the Newton polygon theorem for
   402	   plane coordinates/weighted peak reduction.
   403	2. Specify the symbolic-book grammar and certify the td-7 replay in parallel;
   404	   this buys an honest landing theorem even if every finiteness idea fails.
   405	3. Build the factor-expanded GGV forest only after the Rank-1 polynomial
   406	   perimeter is pinned; carry paired residuals and do not transport through the
   407	   later Laurent map.
   408	4. Run the trace moments as the cheapest residue-A sidecar. Use the higher-row
   409	   data already being generated only as regression for the symbolic selector
   410	   theorem, not as a duplicate solver lane.
   411	5. Run the passport/group pilot before attempting the hard block-descent
   412	   geometry; a persistent primitive \(A_d/S_d\) family can kill Rank 4 cheaply.
   413	
   414	The deliberate non-idea is a Hamiltonian-LND shortcut. For
   415	\(D_f=f_y\partial_x-f_x\partial_y\), one has \(D_f(g)=-1\), but \(D_f\) is
   416	locally nilpotent exactly when \((f,g)\) is already an automorphism. Indeed, if
   417	it were LND, \(-g\) would be a slice; the slice theorem and
   418	\(\ker D_f=\mathbb C[h]\) would give \(\mathbb C[x,y]=\mathbb C[h,g]\).
   419	Writing \(f=P(h)\), the identity
   420	\(1=J(f,g)=P'(h)J(h,g)\) forces \(P\) linear. The converse is
   421	\(D_f=-\partial_g\) in coordinates \((f,g)\).
   422	
   423	There is also a direct boundary witness. At any finite-\(g\) puncture, if
   424	\(g-c\sim ut^e\) and a coordinate \(z\sim vt^{-m}\), then
   425	
   426	\[
   427	 D_f^N z\sim \frac{v}{(eu)^N}
   428	   \prod_{j=0}^{N-1}(m+je)t^{-m-Ne}\ne0.
   429	\]
   430	
   431	Thus any actual realization of residue-A's pinned finite-\(g\) B/x punctures
   432	certifies the opposite of the hoped-for lowering filtration; that avenue is
   433	killed before it enters the ranked list.

