     6	
     7	**BLOCKED. No upper bound on `td` is proved by FC5, the `M=1` depth
     8	closure, and NF-M as presently stated.** More sharply, their explicitly
     9	extracted scalar bookkeeping consequences do not force
    10	
    11	\[
    12	  \sum_{P\in T_{a,\mathrm{pole}}}\frac{a_Pb_P}{\nu_P}\le 1,
    13	\]
    14	
    15	and they do not force any weaker finite bound on that sum, even with the
    16	global Sigray type fixed to \((\alpha,\beta)=(2,3)\), when their displayed
    17	local consequences are treated as the bookkeeping system. This is not a
    18	logical-independence claim about the full hypotheses “actual Keller pair”
    19	and “actual Eggers--Wall tree”; it identifies the global content that any
    20	proof must still use.
    21	
    22	This is not merely failure to find the right manipulation. There is an
    23	explicit infinite **formal arithmetic-schema family** below. Its sheet
    24	numbers are `td = 4A -> infinity`; it satisfies the pole laws, N1, all
    25	displayed numerical equations of a Proposition 9.3 case-IIa schema, FC5,
    26	separately solvable local coefficient identities, the numerical case-IV
    27	terminal conditions, and non-conflict between the proved charge lower bound
    28	and the global ceiling. The family stays entirely on
    29	`M=2 -> M=3`, outside the scope of the `M=1` depth theorem. NF-M sees one
    30	coefficient type for each member. What is not proved is a compatible local
    31	chart transition, global Eggers--Wall gluing, or realization by one
    32	polynomial Keller pair.
    33	
    34	Accordingly:
    35	
    36	- **PROVED:** the exact pole-mass potential carried by an entry state is
    37	  \(\Phi_s(w,M)=wM^2/(sM-1)\), where \(s=\alpha+\beta\).
    38	- **PROVED:** FC5 is a local frame identity. It has no incoming-mass term.
    39	- **PROVED:** the natural potential \(\Phi_s\) changes with both signs on
    40	  coefficient-solvable local merge charts, so it is not a monotone
    41	  one-step telescope.
    42	- **PROVED:** nonsaturated all-\(\mu=1\) IIa merges are locally
    43	  \(\Phi_s\)-dissipative. This is genuine positive structure, but it points
    44	  in the wrong direction for an upper bound on leaf mass.
    45	- **PROVED:** depth closure gives a finite cumulative jump-cell menu and
    46	  NF-M gives finite isolated coefficient-type counts after fixing their
    47	  respective inputs; neither is coercive in `td`.
    48	- **CONJECTURE:** the sharp target is the normalized mismatch-energy bound
    49	  on a common resolution. A proof needs new global Keller/proximity
    50	  information, not another emission identity.
    51	- **CORRECTION TO THE STATED PAYOFF:** even the sharp mass bound gives only
    52	  `td <= alpha*beta`. The repository has no absolute finite GGV type list.
    53	  Thus TD-BOUND alone does not make the ladder cofinal.
    54	
    55	There is a second, elementary correction of principle: a universal absolute
    56	bound `td <= N` for *every* plane Keller counterexample would already prove
    57	the two-dimensional Jacobian conjecture, because iterating one counterexample
    58	would give sheet numbers `td^k`. A finite bound useful as an intermediate
    59	book theorem must therefore be restricted to a class not closed under
    60	iteration. Bounding a specially selected globally minimal counterexample is
    61	the reduction-relevant option; bounding primitive/indecomposable
    62	representatives would be another possible quantifier.
    63	
    64	All gaps below are explicitly labelled **CONJECTURE**. A “formal family” is
    65	never asserted to be a Keller counterexample.
