    69	## 1. Notation and the exact content of FC5
    70	
    71	Use \((\alpha,\beta)\), with \(2\le\alpha<\beta\) and
    72	\(\gcd(\alpha,\beta)=1\), for the Sigray type. Put
    73	
    74	\[
    75	  s:=\alpha+\beta.
    76	\]
    77	
    78	The letter `r` below denotes the number of arrivals at a merge, never the
    79	first component of the type. At a nonterminal chart \(G\), write
    80	
    81	\[
    82	 X_G:=D_G/i_G,\qquad P_G=i_Gd_p,\qquad
    83	 \rho_G:=D_G/P_G,\qquad
    84	 w_G:=\frac{\bar\kappa_G-\rho_G}{\nu_G}.
    85	\]
    86	
    87	The full-degree normalization is recorded in
    88	[`xmodel/sol-normalform.md:100-120`](sol-normalform.md). The general merge
    89	handshake and ratio law are in
    90	[`BOOK-OFFAXIS.md:293-331`](../BOOK-OFFAXIS.md).
    91	
    92	### Proposition 1 (FC5 reconstructed)
    93	
    94	**PROVED.** The equal-quotient/Proposition 9.3 ratio equation is
    95	
    96	\[
    97	  \frac{X_G}{\bar\kappa_G}=\frac{d_p}{d_q}.
    98	\]
    99	
   100	Since \(P_G=i_Gd_p\),
   101	
   102	\[
   103	 \rho_G=\frac{D_G}{P_G}=\frac{X_G}{d_p}
   104	       =\frac{\bar\kappa_G}{d_q}.
   105	\]
   106	
   107	Consequently
   108	
   109	\[
   110	 \boxed{
   111	 w_G=\frac{\bar\kappa_G(d_q-1)}{\nu_Gd_q}},
   112	 \qquad
   113	 \boxed{M_G=\gcd(d_p,d_q)}.                         \tag{1.1}
   114	\]
   115	
   116	This is exactly FC5 as certified in
   117	[`TOWER-TD11.md:695-719`](../TOWER-TD11.md) and implemented at
   118	[`cases/td11_census.py:1064-1120`](../cases/td11_census.py).
   119	
   120	For an NF-M schema,
   121	
   122	\[
   123	 d_p=\epsilon+\nu\sum_i p_if_i,
   124	 \qquad d_q=1+\nu\widehat Q,
   125	\]
   126	
   127	so (1.1) becomes
   128	
   129	\[
   130	 w_G=\frac{\bar\kappa_G\widehat Q}{d_q},\qquad
   131	 M_G=\gcd\!\left(\epsilon+\nu\sum_i p_if_i,
   132	                  1+\nu\widehat Q\right).            \tag{1.2}
   133	\]
   134	
   135	The orbit locations and coefficient type do not occur. That is useful for
   136	state emission, but it is also the loss of information that prevents FC5
   137	from being a conservation law.
   138	
   139	### Exact scope
   140	
   141	Equation (1.1) says what state a chart emits after its frame is already
   142	known. It contains:
   143	
   144	- no number of incoming pole leaves;
   145	- no incoming \((a,b,\nu)\)-mass;
   146	- no charge accumulated above the chart;
   147	- no proximity multiplicity or intersection defect;
   148	- no coefficient/root positions; and
   149	- no relation between distinct charts.
   150	
   151	Also, only \(M_G=\gcd(d_p,d_q)\) is unconditional. The frequently used
   152	divisibility \(M_G\mid\sum\mu_e\) has the restricted
   153	`epsilon=0=k` scope described in `BOOK-OFFAXIS.md:317-331`.
   154	
   155	Thus FC5 is **PROVED as an identity**, not as a conservation or monotonicity
   156	statement.
   157	
