  1196	## Conclusion
  1197	
  1198	The merged-emission law is valuable as a deterministic transition rule, but
  1199	it is not the missing global accountant. Its exact pole-mass interface is
  1200	\(\Phi_s\); that potential is nonmonotone on coefficient-solvable local
  1201	charts. More decisively, the extracted arithmetic relaxation admits an
  1202	arbitrarily large fixed-type scale with constant FC5 output. Depth closure
  1203	and NF-M then quotient what remains only after the unbounded entry/schema
  1204	parameters have been fixed.
