   371	### B.1 Boxed PCC is sufficient for `td <= alpha*beta`. CONFIRMED.
   372	
   373	Setup: dominant nonautomorphic Sigray-normalized Keller pair,
   374	coprime type \(2\le\alpha<\beta\), \(d=B\alpha\), \(e=B\beta\),
   375	pencils \(\mathcal L_f=\langle F,Z^d\rangle\),
   376	\(\mathcal L_g=\langle G,Z^e\rangle\), \(\pi:X\to\mathbb P^2\) the
   377	minimal simultaneous point resolution making both maps morphisms.
   378	\(R_p,S_p\) are orders of mobile strict transforms of generic
   379	members, in the orthogonal total-transform point basis, zero when
   380	\(p\) is not a base center of that pencil.
   381	
   382	Generic fiber classes (1.4) have \(C^2=D^2=0\) because they are
   383	fibers of morphisms to \(\mathbb P^1\). The Bézout identities
   384	(1.5) are the expansion of those squares and of \(C\cdot D\) in
   385	the orthogonal basis \((H,E_p^*)\), \((E_p^*)^2=-1\).
   386	
   387	The identification \(C\cdot D=\mathrm{td}\) is the one-sentence
   388	step. It is standard and is not a cheat: after both pencils are
   389	resolved, a generic pair of **finite** target values is not
   390	attained on \(Z=0\) (every point of \(F=Z=0\) is a base point of
   391	\(\mathcal L_f\), similarly for \(G\)), and residual intersections
   392	of proper transforms are the affine generic fiber of \((f,g)\), of
   393	degree \(\mathrm{td}\). Characteristic zero makes the extension
   394	separable. A hostile reading can still call the sentence a sketch
   395	rather than a written intersection-theory lemma; it is the same
   396	sketch already accepted at
   397	`xmodel/grok-k-g5-review.md:525-533,579-583`, now with the cluster
   398	and point-basis conventions pinned so that a further blowup after
   399	both pencils are resolved adds zero generic multiplicities and
   400	does not change (1.2). That pinning is a tightening, not a
   401	weakening to a tautology. Not enough to withhold CONFIRMED.
   402	
   403	Floors: \(R_p,S_p\) are nonnegative integers, so
   404	\(R_p\ge\alpha h_p\), \(S_p\ge\beta h_p\), and
   405	\(R_p S_p\ge\alpha\beta h_p^2\) termwise, including the cases
   406	\(h_p=0\) and the cases where \(p\) belongs to only one cluster.
   407	Summing and invoking PCC:
   408	
   409	\[
   410	B^2\alpha\beta-\mathrm{td}
   411	=\sum R_p S_p
   412	\ge\alpha\beta\sum h_p^2
   413	\ge\alpha\beta(B^2-1),
   414	\]
   415	
   416	hence \(\mathrm{td}\le\alpha\beta\). No converse is used or
   417	claimed. Jacobian constancy is used only to place the pair in the
   418	Keller/Sigray setup (so \(\mathrm{td}\) is defined and finite);
   419	the inequality itself is intersection-theoretic.
