./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/grok-normalform-review.md:150:  **Independence, as stated.** Without NF-Z there is unbounded zero-cost depth at frozen charged skeleton and frozen coefficients. Without NF-P there is an unbounded characteristic at one charged vertex, plus unclassified `ν=1` merges. Without NF-M there is unclassified coefficient data after every integer parameter is frozen. None of those three sentences is discharged by either of the other two, or by depth / N1–N4 / P3 / the 11-A 2-adic. The “independent relative to the cited kernels” claim is correct.
