   113	## 3. State and primitive transformations (exact semantics)
   114	
   115	**State** = (SuppP, SuppQ, Consts, Certs, Log), where SuppP/SuppQ are corner
   116	lists of lattice polygons in ℤ² (Laurent allowed: x-exponents may be negative;
   117	everything lives in L^(1) = K[x,x^{−1},y]); while P,Q are proportional the state
   118	stores one 1/m-polygon S with SuppP = m·S, SuppQ = n·S (they individuate only at
   119	the tail-resolution step). Consts = symbolic scalars (λ, α_i, …) each carrying
   120	constraints from its introduction (≠0, mutual distinctness, "root of the edge
   121	form with multiplicity t·qm"). Certs = active edge-form certificates. Log =
   122	append-only justifications (rule id + verified hypotheses + branch labels).
   123	
   124	Primitive ops (all exact on support sets; each records its bracket effect):
   125	
   126	- **T-swap** φ₁: (i,j) ↦ (j,i). Bracket ↦ −bracket (absorb into scalar).
   127	- **T-shift** e_K(λ): x ↦ x, y ↦ y + λx^{−K}, K ∈ ℕ. Automorphism of L^(1);
   128	  bracket invariant. Naive support map: (i,j) ↦ {(i−Kt, j−t) : 0 ≤ t ≤ j}.
   129	  Cancellation beyond the naive map happens ONLY on an edge covered by a
   130	  certificate (below); elsewhere take the union/hull. Valid for cutting an
   131	  edge of direction (ρ,σ) only when ρ = 1 after normalization, i.e. (1,−K)
   132	  (else x^{−σ/ρ} ∉ L^(1); e.g. the (2,−7) branch of 4.3 is uncuttable and
   133	  simply terminates as case a)). Only ever applied when a certificate names λ.
   134	- **T-const**: add constants / scale by K^× (keeps (0,0) in supports; scales
   135	  bracket).
   136	- **T-final** ψ_j: x ↦ x^{−1}, y ↦ x^j y: (i,j') ↦ (j·j'−i, j'). Injective on
   137	  supports (no cancellation possible); precondition: j·j'−i ≥ 0 on all support
   138	  (choice of j) and all (i,0) have i ≤ 0. Bracket ↦ −x^{j−2}·bracket.
   139	
   140	**Edge-form certificate** (the only place coefficient information enters):
   141	for an edge E of direction (1,−K) (in cutting position) with en(E) = m·A,
   142	a certificate is
   143	`ℓ_{1,−K}(P) = λ_P · x^{c} y^{d} · Π_i (z−λ_i)^{q·m·t_i}`, z := x^K y,
   144	with (c,d) = m·st-corner data, Σt_i = z-degree/q·m, λ_i distinct, nonzero.
   145	Applying e_K(λ₁) to a certified edge rewrites it exactly:
   146	(z−λ₁) ↦ z, (z−λ_i) ↦ (z−(λ_i−λ₁)), y^d ↦ (y+λ₁x^{−K})^d, giving new edge
   147	support st′ = st + qm·t₁·(K,1) (shorten), or full collapse to en when the
   148	partition is trivial (one root, d = 0); the (y+λ₁x^{−K})^d factor contributes
   149	the Laurent tail corners {(c−K·d̃, 0)-direction points, d̃ ≤ d} — in practice a
   150	provisional corner (i_st − K·d, 0), refined later by tail resolution.
   151	
   152	## 4. Rule library (each rule = checkable preconditions ⇒ conclusion)
   153	
   154	R1 **Edge power (GGV1 Cor 7.4 / 7.2).** Preconditions, verified on the state:
   155	   [P,Q] ∈ K^× still (i.e. before T-final); v-ratios m/n at (1,1),(0,1) (resp.
   156	   (1,0)); (ρ₀,σ₀) ∈ Dir(P), v_{ρ₀,σ₀}(P) > 0; (1/m)st (resp. en) = (a/l,b) ∈
   157	   (1/l)ℤ×ℕ with b < a/l (7.4) or b > a/l (7.2); F-data st/en(F) = (p/q)(a/l,b)
   158	   with p,q coprime — supplied by (q_k) from the chain. Conclusion: for every
   159	   (ρ,σ) strictly between (ρ₀,σ₀) and the bounding direction (ρ̃,σ̃):
   160	   ℓ_{ρ,σ}(P) = λR^{qm}, R (ρ,σ)-homogeneous. Corollary used constantly:
   161	   en(R) = (1/(qm))·en of that edge must be a LATTICE point, and R's support
   162	   lies on the segment [st(R), en(R)] with spacing gap-divisibility
   163	   (GGV2 Remark `gap`: only exponents divisible by gap(ρ,l) occur).
   164	R2 **q from chain data (GGV5 (q_k)).** q = v_{ρ,σ}(A_h)/gcd(ρ+σ, v_{ρ,σ}(A_h))
   165	   at (ρ,σ) = dir(A_h−A_h′). Pure integer arithmetic.
   166	R3 **Predecessor/start filter (GGV22 Algorithm 1 = `PossibleStartingPoints`;
   167	   GGV2 Prop 3.12; GGV6 Prop 2.5).** Input corner (a/l,b); output finite list of
   168	   (c/l,d) that can be st of the next edge, via s := (ρa+σlb)/gcd(ρa+σlb,
   169	   l(ρ+σ)) and the test `(s | N₂ and d>0) or s ≤ N₁`, N₁ = gcd(a−c, b−d),
   170	   N₂ = gcd(c,d). This is implementable verbatim from the paper's pseudocode.
   171	R4 **Forced-multiplicity kill (GGV2 Prop 3.12(2)).** When the direction
   172	   equation (ρ,σ) = −dir(t′·st(R)+ϑ(1,1)) has a solution with ϑ ≤ N₁,
   173	   some linear factor of r(z) has multiplicity exactly ϑ ⇒ kills root
   174	   partitions lacking a ϑ-multiplicity factor (e.g. 4.2: ϑ = s = 6 kills the
   175	   3-distinct-roots partition of R = x²·(z-cubic)).
   176	R5 **Zero-root exclusion (λ₁ ≠ 0).** Assume λ₁ = 0 ⇒ st of the edge moves ⇒
   177	   re-run R3 on the hypothetical support ⇒ derive Pred ≤ (1,−3)-type bound ⇒
   178	   contradiction with R6. Support-level reasoning only.
   179	R6 **x-degree floor (vdE Prop 10.2.6).** P ∈ K[x,y] counterexample ⇒
   180	   deg_x P(x,0) ≥ 1: the support must contain (d,0), d ≥ 1 (pre-Laurent
   181	   stages). Kills candidate shapes whose lower side retracts past x¹.
   182	R7 **PLLC checks (GGV2 `cota`, `casos imposibles`; GGV2 Prop 3.29 / Rem 3.31
   183	   route used for (8,32)).** A last lower corner (a,b) needs b < a,
   184	   b ≤ (a−b−1)², and (a,b) ∉ ℘(n′,n′−1). Used to kill branches whose cut
   185	   would create a forbidden last corner; also powers the (8,32)-style instant
   186	   discard (a bonus capability of the same engine).
   187	R8 **Divisibility of d (GGV1 Thm 7.6(5)(8)).** q_h | d_i for later regular
   188	   corners; with d·st(R) primitive-vector arithmetic this pins d₀ (used in
   189	   GGV22's (8,32) discard: q₁ = 4 | d₀ and d₀ ≤ 4 ⇒ d₀ = 4 ⇒ edge form
   190	   (λ x²y⁷(y−λ₁))^{4m}).
   260	   integrality of mandated corners; en(R) lattice test in R1; v_{ρ,σ}-consistency
   261	   v(P)+v(Q) ≥ v([P,Q]) + ρ+σ; bracket bookkeeping (composition of recorded
   262	   factors equals x^{j−2} at emit); (0,0) ∈ both supports; Cor 7.4 hypotheses
   263	   logged with numeric witnesses.
   264	G4 **Cross-check lane (optional, expensive).** For a solved family, Generator A
   265	   on the UNREDUCED rectangle (cases/unreduced.py) and on the reduced output
