   272	
   273	## 8. Steps that require symbolic work on coefficients — honest list
   274	
   275	The good news (established by the traces): for §4-class families the loop never
   276	needs the VALUES of λ, α_i — only their existence, distinctness pattern, and
   277	multiplicities. All kills are integer-arithmetic (R2–R9). What remains genuinely
   278	symbolic, and how to handle it:
   279	
   280	1. **The λ's of each cut**: introduced existentially by certificates; consumed
   281	   by exactly one e_K. Handling: symbolic tokens with constraint sets; no
   282	   arithmetic. Risk case (not hit in §4): two certificates sharing a root
   283	   (would need relations between tokens) — detect and go `stuck`.
   284	2. **Root multiplicity patterns** (B1): combinatorial enumeration + R4/R5
   285	   filters; the "one or two linear factors" analysis of 4.3's proof is exactly
   286	   GGV1 Prop 2.11(3) (a qm-th power with ≤ F-factor bound) + gap-divisibility;
   287	   encode as: #distinct roots ≤ #factors(F̄) with multiplicities ≡ 0 mod m
   288	   — integer-level, but the RULE must be implemented faithfully per hypothesis.
   289	3. **λ₁ ≠ 0 side-conditions** (R5): implemented as sub-searches deriving
   290	   support contradictions; no coefficient computation, but requires the
   291	   recursive engine to be reentrant on hypothetical states.
   292	4. **Aligned-end eliminations** (B3/R9): direction-clash detection = exact
   293	   rational geometry; no coefficients.
   294	5. **Out of scope / future**: GGV6 Thm 7.3 intersection-number discards
   295	   (Puiseux/approximate-root data, genuinely analytic-symbolic) — not needed to
   296	   REDUCE a family, only to discard some without solving; keep as a manual or
   297	   later module.
