+## 7. Conditional proof of WTC-1
+
+### Theorem 7.1 — WTC-1 reduced to three conjectures
+
+Assume WTC-CHART, WTC-ORD, and WTC-DEN.  Then every certified paired packet
+determines a named proper or infinitely-near common base center \(p\) of the
+minimal simultaneous pencil resolution, its immediate proximity parent or
+parents, and the exact mobile multiplicities (0.1).  The construction is
+functorial under the next certified Laurent cut.
+
+#### Proof
+
+Theorem 2.1 supplies the same-core paired powers and hence the integers
+\(A=q\alpha t,C=q\beta t\).  WTC-CHART supplies the regular point \(p\), the
+boundary equalities (3.11), the four weak local generators, the blowup word,
+and the successor/root identifier.  WTC-ORD is exactly the pair of transverse
+ladders in (4.8), while WTC-DEN is exactly the other pair of inequalities.
+Corollary 4.3 therefore gives
+
+\[
+R_p=A=q\alpha t,qquad S_p=C=q\beta t,qquad h_p=qt.
+\]
+
+Lemma 4.4 places \(p\) in the canonical minimal simultaneous base cluster and
+identifies its proximity parents.  The successor compatibility is the fourth
+clause of WTC-CHART. \(\square\)
+
+This theorem is a genuine reduction: the remaining three conjectures are
+logically independent at the local-data level.  WTC-CHART names the ordinary
+maximal ideal, Proposition 5.1 separates WTC-ORD from the packet, and
+Proposition 5.2 separates WTC-DEN from WTC-ORD.
+
+---
+
+## 8. What the bank contributes—and cannot contribute
+
+### 8.1 Corollary 7.4 and Section 4
+
+The exact gain is Theorem 2.1.  The automated certificate stores
+
+\[
+\ell_{1,-K}(P)=\lambda_Px^cy^d
+  \prod_i(z-\lambda_i)^{qmt_i},\qquad z=x^Ky,            \tag{8.1}
+\]
+
+and the cut shifts one selected root to zero.  This supplies direction, root
+token, and multiplicity.  It does not store:
+
+- the paired \(Q\)-factor as a first-class certificate;
+- \(F,G,Z^d,Z^e\) as projective sections;
+- exceptional fixed divisors;
+- the transverse coefficient polynomials in (4.4)/(4.7);
+- a center identifier or proximity parents; or
+- relations between root tokens in different certificates.
+
+Indeed shared-root relations currently force the Section-4 engine to stop:
+`SECTION4-AUTOMATION.md:273-283`.  The support-level transformations in
+`lib/reduce4.py` are faithful to their stated scope but cannot check (4.8).
+
+### 8.2 The normalization transport theorem
+
+`TRANSPORT.md` proves the pre-Laurent GGV-to-Sigray normalization and an exact
+rational valuation ledger.  It explicitly says that it is not a
+corner-to-tree functor, does not apply to the post-Laurent bracket objects, and
+does not determine pole/fiber decorations (`TRANSPORT.md:3-12,452-463`).  Its
+remaining `CONJECTURE T` is closely related to WTC-CHART, but even a complete
+corner-to-tree functor would not by itself prove the ordinary ladders or
+denominator capacity.
+
+### 8.3 FC5
+
+FC5 is exactly
+
+\[
+w_G=\frac{\bar\kappa_G(d_q-1)}{\nu_Gd_q},
+\qquad M_G=\gcd(d_p,d_q).                               \tag{8.2}
+\]
+
+It consumes an already fixed local frame and emits two scalars.  It has no
+root position, exceptional divisor, transverse jet, incoming point-basis
+mass, proximity relation, or cross-chart identifier.  Its noninjectivity is
+visible in the banked BB2 family
+
+\[
+(\bar\kappa,d_p,d_q)=(6N+3,4N+1,2N+1),                 \tag{8.3}
+\]
+
+for which every \(N\) emits \((w,M)=(6,1)\).  See
+`xmodel/sol-g5-emission.md:92-156,332-359` and
+`cases/td11_census.py:1061-1120`.
+
+Thus FC5 is useful as a scalar consistency check *after* a center certificate
+exists.  It cannot produce that certificate or prove a divisibility in (6.1).
+
+### 8.4 NF-M and the census infrastructure
+
+NF-M bounds coefficient types only after the discrete schema and emitted
+frame have been fixed; its future-locality statement requires the same type
+and the same frame.  It neither names a projective point nor equates GGV root
+occurrences across charts (`NF-M.md:95-122`).
+
+The normal-form fat record and the censuses do retain useful arithmetic,
+root-orbit, arrival, scale, and local coefficient information.  They do not
+retain the four projective sections, the ordinary maximal ideal, exceptional
+valuations, point-basis coefficients, or proximity.  Several public book keys
+also deliberately aggregate different entries/contexts; the td-11 output is
+an instrument-uniform death quotient, not a literal extension or occurrence
+census.  Relevant audits are:
+
+- `xmodel/sol-normalform.md:74-120,610-698`;
+- `cases/book_enum.py:283-305,373-386`;
+- `xmodel/sol-census-final.md:5-15,56-67`;
+- `xmodel/sol-census-review.md:125-157`; and
+- `TDBOUND.md:29-33`.
+
+Accordingly, neither the 21-of-22 construction frequency nor an NF-M type
+count is a center-coverage statement.  This confirms the negative conclusion
+at `xmodel/sol-pcc-orbits.md:354-478`.
+
+### 8.5 Productive use of the existing infrastructure
+
+The current exact-arithmetic and fail-closed machinery can check enriched
+certificates.  A minimally adequate new record is:
+
+```text
+CenterPacketCertificate
+  source_pair_id; exact Corollary-7.4 hypotheses
+  cut_prefix; primitive direction; q
+  root_token; Kummer_orbit; root multiplicity t
+  regular_fan; unimodular chart matrices; point-blowup word
+  exceptional_components_through_p; proximity_parent_ids
+  pullback valuations of F, Z^d, G, Z^e
+  fixed divisors Delta_f, Delta_g
+  local generators A_f, B_f, A_g, B_g
+  transverse quotients a_j / r^(A-j), c_j / r^(C-j)
+  denominator orders; capacity N
+  canonical center_id; successor occurrence ids
+  emitted R_p, S_p; FC5 consistency fields
+```
+
+A gate should reject the record unless:
+
+1. the graph maps compose exactly to the Laurent word;
+2. the four section pullbacks and fixed divisors replay;
+3. the two boundary packets replay;
+4. every transverse division in (6.1) has zero remainder;
+5. both capacity inequalities replay; and
+6. parent and successor identifiers agree under chart overlap/descent.
+
+This would certify WTC for a *given realized packet*.  It would not prove the
+uniform Keller conjectures or the occurrence coverage needed by PCC.
+
